Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.56,0:00:08.50,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,Our world is host to creatures threatening \Nhumanity that we call monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.98,0:00:12.60,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,To protect people from these monsters,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.60,0:00:17.95,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,we need those with the sacred \Npower to create barriers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.63,0:00:22.37,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,These women are saints.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.09,0:00:26.81,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,They drive back the monsters \Nand purify the land.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.81,0:00:30.30,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,Their presence is such \Na boon to national security
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.30,0:00:37.49,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,that it is vital to every country\Nto have at least one saint.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.80,0:00:42.41,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,And this land, the Kingdom of Girtonia,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.41,0:00:47.93,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,is home to the woman known as the greatest \Nsaint of all time, Philia Adenauer.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.65,0:00:52.36,Default,Man 1,0,0,0,,Oh, Saint Philia is back?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.36,0:00:55.76,Default,Man 2,0,0,0,,Right. She went to vanquish monsters\N in the northwest, didn't she?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.76,0:00:58.24,Default,Man 3,0,0,0,,Saint Philia to the rescue as usual, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.24,0:01:00.96,Default,Man 3,0,0,0,,I reckon that's what makes her\Nthe "greatest ever" or whatnot.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.96,0:01:05.72,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,Philia Adenauer is the perfect saint.\NThere is nothing she cannot do.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.72,0:01:08.80,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,However, there is one respect \Nin which she is lacking.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.80,0:01:11.72,Default,Mother,0,0,0,,That's the saint!\NGo on. You'd better not offend her.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.72,0:01:14.42,Default,Boy,0,0,0,,G-Good day, Saint Philia.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.39,0:01:17.56,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,And that is...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.12,0:01:22.50,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,her smile.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.99,0:01:26.33,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Good day.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:28.83,0:01:34.17,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,To be a saint is to be a wellspring \Nof love, cherished by her people.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.50,0:01:36.20,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(710,1)\fnGeorgia\fs8\shad0\blur4\c&H5F6156&\3c&HEFF5F2&\b1\pos(515.369,270.367)}The Kingdom of Girtonia's 28th Saint\N{\fs14}Philia Adenauer
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.64,0:01:41.13,Main - Italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,But Philia is a saint who never smiled.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.31,0:01:49.00,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)\blur4\t(1,500,\blur0)\an8\fnGeorgia\b1\fs18\shad0\bord0\c&H884FD9&}The Too-Perfect Saint{\c&H9B9999&}: {\c&HDEC58D&}Tossed {\c&HDDBF93&}Aside\N{\c&HE2B99A&}by {\c&HC8ACAD&}My {\c&HDDB3B4&}Fiancé {\c&HDCBAC3&}and {\c&HD79BB3&}Sold {\c&HCEA8CE&}to {\c&HD4A8D5&}Another {\c&HC3A8E2&}Kingdom
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.33,0:01:54.55,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(690,1)\shad1\bord.\fnGeorgia\fs10\pos(511.693,274.041)\c&HF9F8FA&\3c&H4E4E4E&\4c&H252526&}Episode 1\N{\fs12}"The {\fs14\b1\c&HE4C594&}S{\c&HFEB59F&}a{\c&HE895B4&}i{\c&HEA77BD&}n{\c&HFB62CD&}t{\fs12\b0\c&HF9F8FA&} Who Never Smiled"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.84,0:01:56.33,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,Come again!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.23,0:02:00.86,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Excuse me, sir. Who might \Nthat beautiful woman be?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.86,0:02:03.40,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,This your first time in Girtonia?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.40,0:02:04.12,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.12,0:02:05.61,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,Guess you wouldn't know, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.61,0:02:07.34,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,She's our saint.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.34,0:02:10.44,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,Girtonia currently has two, in fact!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.94,0:02:14.00,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,The other is Saint Mia!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.00,0:02:17.00,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,She's so sweet and darling!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.00,0:02:23.12,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,The smile she blesses the people of Girtonia\Nwith equally is truly a national treasure!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.12,0:02:27.29,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,The kind, charming Saint Mia is beloved by all!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.60,0:02:30.75,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,But that one over there...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.29,0:02:37.05,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,That's Saint Philia, Saint Mia's elder sister\Nand purportedly the most gifted in history.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.05,0:02:38.58,Default,Merchant,0,0,0,,Saint Philia!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.58,0:02:40.63,Default,Merchant,0,0,0,,About my request from the other day...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.63,0:02:44.89,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,The shipping route has been \Nsecured. You can rest easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.89,0:02:46.50,Default,Old Lady,0,0,0,,Saint Philia.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.50,0:02:48.93,Default,Old Lady,0,0,0,,Our crops are dying from this drought.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.93,0:02:51.49,Default,Old Lady,0,0,0,,Can't you please make it rain?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.49,0:02:54.57,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Yes, I performed the ritual recently.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.57,0:02:56.48,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,It should rain very soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.48,0:03:00.49,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,I believe I can arrange for regular\N rainfall in the future as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.88,0:03:02.36,Default,Merchant,0,0,0,,{\i1}She can do that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.36,0:03:04.64,Default,Doctor,0,0,0,,Well, well, if it isn't our precious saint.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.64,0:03:08.16,Default,Doctor,0,0,0,,I wanted to check in about that \Nmedicine I asked you to develop.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.50,0:03:11.30,Default,Doctor,0,0,0,,{\i1}I gave her an impossible task!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.30,0:03:13.08,Default,Doctor,0,0,0,,{\i1}She could never pull it off, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.08,0:03:16.21,Default,Doctor,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now, admit your failure\N and beg for forgiveness!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.21,0:03:19.93,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,I gave the formula to the herbalist just now.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.93,0:03:21.26,Default,Doctor,0,0,0,,You pulled it off?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.95,0:03:25.01,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Sounds like Girtonia's saint is amazing.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:25.35,0:03:29.77,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,Yeah. Most of Girtonia's land\Nis either desert or barren.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.77,0:03:39.65,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnArial\fs16\b1\shad0\move(134.431,60.98,-98.431,60.98)\frz21.04\c&H1C461F&\3c&H8DCE8D&}Examples of Philia's Achievements
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.77,0:03:39.65,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\an1\fnArial\fs12\shad0\move(170,125.878,-65,125.878)\b1\c&H1F3A3B&\3c&HD1FFFD&}Developing new medicines
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.77,0:03:39.65,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fnArial\fs12\shad0\move(170,175.878,-65,175.878)\b1\c&H1F3A3B&\3c&HD1FFFD&}Advancements in pharmacology
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.77,0:03:39.65,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fnArial\fs12\shad0\b1\c&H1F3A3B&\3c&HD1FFFD&\move(397.263,231.061,162.263,231.061)}Subsequently establishing\Ntrade routes
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.77,0:03:39.65,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\an1\fnArial\fs12\shad0\move(398,120,163,120)\b1\c&H1F3A3B&\3c&HD1FFFD&}Expanding safe zones\Nwith powerful barriers
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.77,0:03:39.65,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\an1\fnArial\fs12\shad0\b1\c&H1F3A3B&\3c&HD1FFFD&\move(590.182,103.837,355.182,103.837)}Developing new farmland
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.77,0:03:39.65,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fnArial\fs12\shad0\b1\c&H1F3A3B&\3c&HD1FFFD&\move(590,185,355,185)}Cultivating more suitable crops
Dialogue: 1,0:03:30.19,0:03:33.97,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,We don't have a lot of natural resources. \NLife used to be real hard.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:33.97,0:03:36.59,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,She's the one who turned everything around.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:36.59,0:03:39.05,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,But she's {\i1}so{\i0} good, \Nshe's stepped on some toes,
Dialogue: 1,0:03:39.05,0:03:41.02,Default,Shopkeep,0,0,0,,so there are folks who resent her, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.25,0:03:46.91,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,I have returned home.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.91,0:03:50.96,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,Philia! How long must you waste\Non such simple tasks?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.26,0:03:54.83,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Please forgive me, Mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.83,0:03:56.98,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,You are utterly incompetent.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.98,0:04:00.30,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,I see why it took you \Nso long to become a saint.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.30,0:04:02.42,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,You should take a lesson from Mia,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.78,0:04:06.92,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,a true genius who completed her \Nsaint training in just one year!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.92,0:04:11.64,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,And unlike you, she has a smile\Nto soothe the souls of all who behold it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.95,0:04:15.69,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,Don't you think {\i1}she's{\i0} far closer\Nto what the people expect of a saint?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.07,0:04:16.89,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.89,0:04:18.69,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,And then we have you!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.69,0:04:21.54,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,Stealing people's work \Njust to prove yourself...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.54,0:04:25.04,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,How haughty and self-concerned\N with looking superior!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.04,0:04:27.44,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,You have the perfect role model at hand,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.44,0:04:30.58,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,so why can't you manage\Neven a mote of charm?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.58,0:04:34.04,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,Do you realize how insistently \Nyou upset those around you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.04,0:04:36.68,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,And you do it all with that\N frighteningly blank expression!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.68,0:04:38.67,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,You shame the title of saint!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.11,0:04:42.40,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,At tea parties, we hear nothing \Nbut complaints about your attitude!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.40,0:04:45.18,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,How do you think that makes {\i1}us{\i0} feel?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.00,0:04:48.80,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Please forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.43,0:04:53.48,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,You should take the time you spend studying\Nmedicine and work on your personality instead!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.48,0:04:57.19,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,What scant praise you received for your \Ntalents doesn't justify such arrogance!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.81,0:05:00.43,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ah, I've done it again...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.94,0:05:04.07,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,The way people see you affects \Nthe way they see Mia, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.07,0:05:06.99,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,Try to behave like her older sister for once.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.76,0:05:11.94,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Yes, Mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.54,0:05:27.51,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}How did things turn out this way?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.43,0:05:32.39,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}A saint's duty is to use\N her power for her kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.07,0:05:36.81,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's what I was taught. And yet...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.07,0:05:41.40,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}The more I've done,\N the harder I've worked...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.84,0:05:45.33,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}For some reason, I've just \Nended up further ostracized.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.60,0:05:49.42,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Be charming? Smile?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.94,0:06:12.05,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't understand any of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.56,0:06:27.07,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've never known how to smile.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.07,0:06:30.82,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps that's what turned\Nmy parents against me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.82,0:06:33.71,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}As I watched them shower\Nmy sister with all their love,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.71,0:06:35.33,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}even as a child, I could tell...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.16,0:06:40.63,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}"I'm going to have to work \Nvery hard to ever be loved."
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.34,0:06:47.84,Main - Italics,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Philia Adenauer...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.84,0:06:51.32,Main - Italics,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Born to the Adenauer family,\Nknown for producing saints.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.32,0:06:54.18,Main - Italics,Osvalt,0,0,0,,She left home to join the church at age five.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.18,0:06:58.10,Main - Italics,Osvalt,0,0,0,,She learned etiquette, past and present,\Nas well as magical and martial arts.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.40,0:07:03.98,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}After I learned I was dull\N and lacking in charm,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.30,0:07:07.36,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I knew I was going to have\N to be exceptional in some way.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.36,0:07:08.61,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\fnComic Sans MS\b1\fs20\shad0\frz25.23\pos(217.11,118.408)\c&HAF5A37&\3c&HF4FFFD&}Survived alone in the mountains for a month.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.32,0:07:11.11,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}My parents enrolled me in saint training,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.61,0:07:09.86,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\fnComic Sans MS\b1\fs20\shad0\c&H0D223C&\3c&HF2FDFC&\frz22.86\pos(176.689,95.143)}Buried alive in the desert.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.86,0:07:11.11,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\an8\fnComic Sans MS\b1\fs20\shad0\c&H212421&\3c&HE8EBE8&\pos(182.813,122.081)\frz23.64}Slept atop a bed of spikes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.52,0:07:15.66,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}and my mentor put me through hell.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.66,0:07:19.91,Flashback,George,0,0,0,,You're so useless and dull. \NThis training is for {\i1}your{\i0} benefit.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.40,0:07:24.92,Flashback,George,0,0,0,,If you can please us all, \Nyou will finally know love.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.78,0:07:29.15,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Become the perfect saint. \NOne who can do anything."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.15,0:07:34.08,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}The days I spent in training hell, \Nin the shadow of that impossible goal...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.08,0:07:36.39,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was in no shape to smile.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.92,0:07:43.44,Main - Italics,Osvalt,0,0,0,,She was certified as a saint at sixteen \Nand declared the greatest of all time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.44,0:07:47.14,Main - Italics,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Now, at nineteen, she's been \Nrecognized by the king
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.14,0:07:52.11,Main - Italics,Osvalt,0,0,0,,and engaged to the second prince\N of Girtonia, Prince Julius...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.72,0:07:53.87,Default,Guard,0,0,0,,Forgive the wait.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.87,0:07:56.56,Default,Guard,0,0,0,,I shall take you to His Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.56,0:07:57.83,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,If you'd be so kind.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.78,0:08:03.33,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Upon my formal engagement\Nto Prince Julius,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.94,0:08:06.84,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought perhaps my efforts \Nhad at last paid off a little.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.30,0:08:09.55,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I thought I had been acknowledged.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.57,0:08:13.63,Default,Boy,0,0,0,,Dad!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.63,0:08:14.09,Default,Dad,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.86,0:08:17.96,Default,Dad,0,0,0,,You came out to meet me?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.96,0:08:20.00,Default,Boy,0,0,0,,Yeah! Welcome home, Dad!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.00,0:08:21.31,Default,Dad,0,0,0,,Thanks, my boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.99,0:08:35.74,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Big Sister! Welcome home!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.15,0:08:35.74,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(360,1)\fnGeorgia\fs8\shad0\blur4\c&H6037DA&\3c&HEFF5F2&\b1\pos(189.551,48.734)}The Kingdom of Girtonia's 29th Saint\N{\fs14}Mia Adenauer
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.72,0:08:38.52,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Thank you, Mia.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.99,0:08:41.68,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,You're reading in my room again?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.68,0:08:44.77,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Your room is so much more relaxing!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.77,0:08:48.75,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,There's just something soothing \Nabout the way it smells!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.75,0:08:51.96,Main - Top,Mia,0,0,0,,It's like you're all around me, \Nand it makes me feel so safe!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.75,0:08:52.88,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't really feel at home here, \Nbut Mia's always welcoming.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.96,0:08:56.42,Main - Top,Mia,0,0,0,,Though I'd never admit that anywhere else.\NThey'd say I'm obsessed with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.88,0:08:55.62,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's the only thing that makes\Ncoming back feel worthwhile.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.23,0:08:59.99,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Oh? Big Sister, what's that box?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.68,0:09:03.44,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,It's, well...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.02,0:09:06.19,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnArial\fs20\b1\shad0\frz5.679\c&H3A2080&\3c&HE3EEF7&\move(473.11,220.775,460.086,215.714)\t(\fs19)}Rose hairpin
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.15,0:09:06.19,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I-Is this for me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.19,0:09:08.67,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Did you buy this, Big Sister?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.36,0:09:10.24,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.86,0:09:16.32,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(430,1)\fnTimes NEw Roman\fs14\an8\c&H56211D&\b1\3c&HDCADA4&\pos(214.048,52.408)\4c&HA76865&}The Product of 10 Years of Studying
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.86,0:09:16.32,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(430,1)\fnTimes NEw Roman\fs14\c&H332D34&\b1\3c&HF7FBF6&\bord1\shad0\4c&HA76865&\pos(226.297,220.163)}A "whatever's edible" and\N"whatever's not hideous" mindset
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.80,0:09:15.78,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,You, who's never cared anything for clothes\Nor food or music or trends?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.97,0:09:18.82,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Yet you got this just for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.34,0:09:25.02,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I'm so happy! I'll treasure it forever!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.02,0:09:26.29,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}So cute.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.61,0:09:31.02,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I know! As thanks, I'll \Npick out an outfit for you!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.02,0:09:33.36,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,How about something for a \Ndate with Prince Julius?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.36,0:09:34.38,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Maybe tomorrow!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.38,0:09:35.26,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Tomorrow?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.74,0:09:41.17,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,As a matter of fact, the prince \Nwants to see me tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.68,0:09:43.82,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,A date? Is it a date?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.38,0:09:45.35,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.77,0:09:47.72,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Well, I can't argue with the prince!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.72,0:09:51.98,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,But let's go shopping on your\N next day off for sure, Big Sister!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.98,0:09:55.24,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Yes, let's. It's a promise.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.24,0:09:58.74,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}My job is hard...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.06,0:10:04.96,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}But with Mia in my life, \NI know I can weather any storm.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.09,0:10:09.36,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,That wretched Philia...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.36,0:10:12.19,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Her attitude is utterly insufferable.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.19,0:10:15.50,Default,Aide 1,0,0,0,,Being called the greatest \Nof all time has made her arrogant,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.50,0:10:19.03,Default,Aide 1,0,0,0,,yet she's only ever vanquished petty monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.03,0:10:23.12,Default,Aide 2,0,0,0,,She's nothing compared \Nto the legendary saint
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.12,0:10:27.60,Default,Aide 2,0,0,0,,who saved the world from the \Nlegendary archdemon Asmodeus!
Dialogue: 1,0:10:27.60,0:10:29.12,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,True enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.91,0:10:30.73,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(170,1)\fnGeorgia\fs8\shad0\blur4\c&H16185D&\3c&HEFF5F2&\b1\pos(492.709,260.571)}The Kingdom of Girtonia's Second Prince\N{\fs14}Julius Girtonia
Dialogue: 1,0:10:29.12,0:10:32.23,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Girtonia doesn't need two saints.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.36,0:10:35.98,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Let's put the plan into action.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.98,0:10:40.99,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an2\fnGeorgia\b1\fs10\shad0\bord0\c&H884FD9&\pos(320,110)}The Too-Perfect Saint{\c&H9B9999&}: {\c&HDEC58D&}Tossed {\c&HDDBF93&}Aside\N{\c&HE2B99A&}by {\c&HC8ACAD&}My {\c&HDDB3B4&}Fiancé {\c&HDCBAC3&}and {\c&HD79BB3&}Sold {\c&HCEA8CE&}to {\c&HD4A8D5&}Another {\c&HC3A8E2&}Kingdom
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.60,0:10:52.21,Default,Boy,0,0,0,,Oh, it's Saint Mia!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.49,0:10:55.19,Default,Mother,0,0,0,,Saint Mia! Do you have the day off?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.19,0:10:56.13,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I do!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.48,0:10:58.42,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,That's why I'm out for a walk.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.59,0:11:02.34,Default,People,0,0,0,,Saint Mia! Hello!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.34,0:11:03.51,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,Excuse me!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.89,0:11:07.56,Default,Girl,0,0,0,,Saint Mia, thank you for all you do for us!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.84,0:11:09.56,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Oh, thank you so much!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.56,0:11:10.75,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,How delightful.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.75,0:11:13.69,Default,Man 1,0,0,0,,Say, Saint Mia, have you done\N something different with your hair?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.37,0:11:15.32,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.11,0:11:23.03,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,The person I admire most \Nin the world gave this to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.45,0:11:30.59,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wonder if you've made it \Nto the castle yet, Big Sister!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.77,0:11:35.17,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Prince Julius...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.62,0:11:38.36,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wonder why he's summoned me so urgently.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.40,0:11:43.68,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's our family's carriage.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.48,0:11:46.44,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is Father here as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.52,0:11:49.85,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Good to see you, Philia!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.56,0:11:54.81,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've never seen him in \Nsuch a good mood before.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.81,0:11:56.11,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I heard what you did.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.11,0:12:01.01,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,You took initiative and vanquished the \Nwerewolves in the northwest all by yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.01,0:12:02.19,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.19,0:12:06.12,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,The soldiers are always complaining \Nabout you taking their jobs.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.12,0:12:09.34,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,You've even given them advice on formations.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.34,0:12:11.58,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,You know that's not a woman's place.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.96,0:12:14.07,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Your Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.96,0:12:17.12,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Are you pleased about something?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.12,0:12:20.51,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's right! \NI just got some great news, in fact.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.44,0:12:23.10,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,What do you think it is?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.98,0:12:26.71,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Philia Adenauer...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.72,0:12:41.78,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Our engagement is officially terminated!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.77,0:12:52.19,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Could you please elaborate, Your Highness?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.76,0:12:53.91,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.91,0:12:57.17,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I've decided to marry Mia instead.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.17,0:13:00.09,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.67,0:13:05.33,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,There's something so inhuman and \Ncharmless about being too perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.33,0:13:09.14,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Saints should just stick to praying.\NYou don't have to be so talented.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.00,0:13:14.64,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though it's because of my lack \Nof charm that I sought to be perfect...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.64,0:13:18.74,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Your little sister Mia is \Nmuch better in that regard!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.74,0:13:22.53,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,She's beautiful, sweet, and has something\Nspecial that makes you want to protect her.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.53,0:13:27.39,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,If you have to marry a saint of the\NAdenauer family, anyone would choose Mia.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.39,0:13:28.82,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,That's all there is to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.64,0:13:33.29,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Have you informed Mia of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.58,0:13:36.04,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,No, not yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.58,0:13:42.63,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,But I could see she was seeking my \Nfavor at that party the other day!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.63,0:13:43.98,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,And besides...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.52,0:13:46.76,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,He said it was official, remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.81,0:13:53.47,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Father, Mother...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.47,0:13:58.24,Default,George,0,0,0,,It was Prince Julius\N who presented us with the idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.24,0:14:00.06,Default,George,0,0,0,,Naturally, we agreed!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.06,0:14:04.30,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,Do amicably withdraw in the name \Nof Mia's happiness, Philia.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.30,0:14:07.65,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,She would make a much \Nbetter queen, after all!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.22,0:14:11.26,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}If...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.16,0:14:16.83,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}If this is what Mia really wants...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.70,0:14:21.50,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}If it would make her happy...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.53,0:14:24.46,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.35,0:14:27.37,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,There's just one problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.37,0:14:31.01,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Mia could potentially refuse \Nout of consideration for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.01,0:14:32.26,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Which is why...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.26,0:14:34.01,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\fs10\shad0\move(156.029,84.245,190.029,84.245)\i1\c&H17212E&\3c&HFDFEFD&}Almburg
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.26,0:14:34.01,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\fs10\shad0\i1\c&H17212E&\3c&HFDFEFD&\move(493.933,253,527.933,253)}Elekana
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.26,0:14:34.01,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\fs12\shad0\c&H17212E&\3c&HFDFEFD&\move(89.11,140.571,123,140.571)}Parnacorta
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.26,0:14:34.01,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\fs12\shad0\c&H17212E&\3c&HFDFEFD&\move(491.483,160.775,526,160.775)}Girtonia
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.26,0:14:35.27,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I've decided to sell you\Nto our neighbors in Parnacorta!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.82,0:14:40.90,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Wh-What do you mean by that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.70,0:14:45.82,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Apparently their only saint \Npassed away suddenly.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.82,0:14:48.65,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I feel bad for them, so I sounded them out...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.65,0:14:53.78,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,"Might you be in need of a saint deemed \Nto be the greatest of all time?"
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.87,0:14:57.86,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,And what do you think they said?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.86,0:15:04.84,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,They came begging for you, offering\Npayment tantamount to our annual budget!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.30,0:15:10.84,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I mean, my goodness! \NTalk about a fabulous deal for everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.84,0:15:14.58,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Plus, when the public finds out I tearfully\Nlet go of my betrothed for my country,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.58,0:15:16.18,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I'll get a surge in support.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.18,0:15:22.34,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I'll grant 30 percent of the profit \Nto the Adenauers along with a peerage.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.34,0:15:26.07,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,And I'm sure Mia will be \Nover the moon to marry me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.07,0:15:30.32,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Indeed, this is going to make {\i1}everyone{\i0} happy!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.89,0:15:35.97,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's going to make... everyone happy?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.33,0:15:46.48,Default,George,0,0,0,,The one thing I can't understand \Nis why they'd pay so much for Philia.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.48,0:15:50.34,Default,George,0,0,0,,It's the first time anyone's seen \Nworth in you. It's almost strange.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.34,0:15:53.56,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,And now our family will enter \Nthe upper echelons of society!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.56,0:15:56.08,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,What a noble self-sacrifice \Nto honor your parents!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.08,0:15:58.99,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,We've done a fine job raising you after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.99,0:16:01.55,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,I suppose you put in a little effort as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.15,0:16:07.32,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've always...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.09,0:16:10.61,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}All I've ever done...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.60,0:16:16.46,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}was to work hard in hopes \Nof earning your approval.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.17,0:16:23.71,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Am I not also your daughter?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.55,0:16:26.50,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,Farewell, Philia.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.87,0:16:30.46,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,I don't imagine we'll ever meet again.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.82,0:16:39.50,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}But then... where will {\i0}I{\i1} find happiness?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.09,0:17:06.77,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I really have been thrown out.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.15,0:17:22.86,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}What should I have done differently?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.14,0:17:30.48,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I guess I'll never know.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.53,0:17:40.03,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's no fixing any of it now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.36,0:17:48.29,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Now, all that money\N we swindled from Parnacorta...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.29,0:17:50.75,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,What should I spend it on?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.07,0:17:56.29,Default,Aide 1,0,0,0,,Perhaps we could erect a golden \Nstatue of you as Girtonia's king!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.29,0:17:58.37,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Really, let's not get ahead of ourselves!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.37,0:18:01.18,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Father is still alive, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.18,0:18:05.27,Default,Aide 1,0,0,0,,But His Majesty has been ill \Nfor quite a long time...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.54,0:18:11.94,Default,Aide 2,0,0,0,,And the first prince, Fernand, has withdrawn \Nfrom the public eye out of fear of your power.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.38,0:18:17.39,Default,Aide 1,0,0,0,,I believe your coronation may \Ncome sooner than you think.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.39,0:18:20.26,Default,Aide 2,0,0,0,,And the moment you become king,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.26,0:18:24.87,Default,Aide 2,0,0,0,,your greatness will propel Girtonia \Nto new heights of prosperity!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.31,0:18:27.02,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Yes, you're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.59,0:18:30.66,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I'll have it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.40,0:18:34.56,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,The throne of Girtonia {\i1}and{\i0} Mia.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.42,0:19:40.59,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}How long was I asleep?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.68,0:19:44.55,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's been so long since I had nothing to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.55,0:19:46.33,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't know what to do with myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.22,0:19:54.83,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\fs10\shad0\i1\c&H17212E&\3c&HFDFEFD&\move(189.55,95.878,242.55,95.878)}Almburg
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.22,0:19:54.83,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\fs10\shad0\i1\c&H17212E&\3c&HFDFEFD&\move(570.488,289.347,623.488,289.347)\N}Elekana
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.22,0:19:54.83,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\fs12\shad0\c&H17212E&\3c&HFDFEFD&\move(113.608,160.163,166.608,160.163)}Parnacorta
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.22,0:19:54.83,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\fs12\shad0\c&H17212E&\3c&HFDFEFD&\move(568.651,183.429,621.651,183.429)}Girtonia
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.67,0:19:49.50,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Parnacorta...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.50,0:19:51.46,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wonder what it's like there.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.46,0:19:54.83,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}They apparently paid a lot for me...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.83,0:19:58.73,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I suppose they'll expect \Nto get their money's worth.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.31,0:20:02.34,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have to be prepared to work like a slave.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.45,0:20:09.57,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's nothing to be gained \Nfrom fretting over it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.54,0:20:15.70,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Even if I'm moving elsewhere, \Nmy duty remains the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.39,0:20:20.42,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I just need to work hard as a saint.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.21,0:20:27.65,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Work hard? Why am I doing that?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.15,0:20:32.87,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Who and what are the saint's duties for?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.91,0:20:40.26,Default,Coachman,0,0,0,,This is as far as we can take you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.26,0:20:43.68,Default,Coachman,0,0,0,,You can get another carriage\Non the other side of the border.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.06,0:20:46.37,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,The border...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.52,0:21:09.64,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,There's a crowd at the \NParnacorta checkpoint?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.79,0:21:21.78,Default,Knights,0,0,0,,Saint Philia has arrived!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.64,0:21:33.64,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Welcome...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.50,0:21:44.97,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,to Parnacorta.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.01,0:21:54.78,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.67,0:23:32.54,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Too-Perfect Saint: Tossed Aside by \NMy Fiancé and Sold to Another Kingdom{\i0}.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.38,0:23:34.97,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Next time, episode 2:
